<title>UK: Chase sets 2-tranche credit card backed bonds.</title>
<headline>Chase sets 2-tranche credit card backed bonds.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following two-tranche credit card backed global issues were announced by lead manager Chase, to be priced on Wednesday.</p>
<p> BORROWER   CHASE CREDIT CARD MASTER TRUST</p>
<p>* * * * *</p>
<p>CLASS A</p>
<p> AMT    $1.15 BLN     SPREAD     +9-10 BP  EXP FINAL   15.FEB.04</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 BASE	 1M LIBOR  LEG FINAL   15.OCT.06</p>
<p> LAST MOODY AAA	 FEES	 35 BP     PAY DATE    24.FEB.97</p>
<p> LAST S&amp;P   AAA</p>
<p>* * * * *</p>
<p>CLASS B</p>
<p> AMT    $95.833 MLN   SPREAD     +28 BP    EXP FINAL   15 MAR.04</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 BASE	 1M LIBOR  LEG FINAL   15.OCT.06</p>
<p> LAST MOODY A2	  FEES	 40 BP     PAY DATE    24.FEB.97</p>
<p> LAST S&amp;P   A</p>
<p>* * * * *</p>
<p>COMMON TERMS</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX	 DENOMS (K) ONE	 SALE LIMITS UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  GOV LAW     NEW YORK</p>
<p> NOTES	SHORT FIRST COUPON</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
